{"schema":1,"pr":{"repo":"ToukoUrsin/junction26-kuitti","number":4,"title":"Answer the review of #2: refuse long notes, test that CSV files stay in their workspace","url":"https://github.com/ToukoUrsin/junction26-kuitti/pull/4","author":"Crashtest author agent","authorIsAgent":true,"baseSha":"55559f75e42757817126fb003058b7ae404ac72b","headSha":"48471fe4a8497a7b4a3cde4b690668d4ce4aa5fc","additions":53,"deletions":2,"files":2,"issue":{"number":3,"title":"Review of #2 sent back: 2 points for the author","url":"https://github.com/ToukoUrsin/junction26-kuitti/issues/3","body":"Readback wrote this issue from a review of #2 that was sent back.\n\nReviewer: Readback team test (script) (invited judge), 2026-11-14 20:25 UTC, commit 55559f7.\n- Invited with the judge link this repository's team gave out. The name is typed by the judge\n- 16 of 16 questions right, 0 wrong tries (at most 3)\n- Planted bug caught on the first read, with the reason\n- 14 of the lines to read closely a minute (under 15)\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n1. `src/lib/invoices.ts:229`: Cutting a note without a word loses what the user typed. Refuse a note over 2000 characters and say so on the page.\n2. `src/routes/invoices.ts:145`: No test keeps the CSV files of two workspaces apart. Add one: a user of another workspace must never get this file.\n\n## What the AI had left open at these lines\n1. The issue says an invoice has a free-text notes field and gives no limit. The code cuts notes to 2000 characters before they are stored, and it shows no message when it cuts.\n2. This line makes the workspace part of the key under which a built CSV file is kept. When the workspace was taken out of the key, a user could download a file that holds the invoices of another workspace, and every test still passed.\n\n## Accepted as they are (5)\n- `src/db.ts:160-187`: The slow-export session added it to get under 500 ms; fine for now, but it needs its own issue.\n- `src/db.ts:151-152`: It is what made the search fast again in session 3, and an index does not change what users see.\n- `src/lib/invoices.ts:372-377`: Owners can revoke the link, and clients need it to keep working after the first open.\n- `src/lib/invoices.ts:385`: The token is 32 random hex characters and the lookup is an exact match on it.\n- `src/routes/share.ts:25`: It is the same total function the signed-in invoice page uses, which has tests.\n\nThe same rulings are in Entire Brain and on the trail of the pull request, where the author agent reads them."}},"intro":"A reviewer sent back two points on the invoice work. This change stops cutting long notes without a word: a note over 2000 characters is now refused with a message, and the typed text stays on the page. It also adds a test that checks a CSV file built for one workspace is never given to a user of another workspace.","stops":[{"id":"long-note-refused","title":"A note over 2000 characters is refused with a message, not cut","why":"Before, the note was cut to 2000 characters before it was stored and the user was not told. The reviewer asked to refuse such a note and say so on the page, so the length is now checked together with the other form rules.","blocks":[{"type":"prose","text":"Notes enter through `readNotes`. It used to end with `.slice(0, MAX_NOTES)`. Look at what it **still does** to the text before it returns it."},{"type":"code","file":"src/lib/invoices.ts","from":227,"to":230,"lines":[{"n":null,"kind":"del","tokens":[["/** Free text from a textarea or JSON: normalised line endings, bounded length. */","comment"]]},{"n":227,"kind":"add","tokens":[["/** Free text from a textarea or JSON: normalised line endings. Length is checked in validateInvoice, never cut. */","comment"]]},{"n":228,"kind":"ctx","tokens":[["export","keyword"],[" ",""],["function","keyword"],[" ",""],["readNotes","function"],["(v",""],[":","keyword"],[" ",""],["unknown","constant"],[")",""],[":","keyword"],[" ",""],["string","constant"],[" {",""]]},{"n":null,"kind":"del","token